{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"152cea25d0188290b7abf5e1824b565bae49bf8edca16345c4efc100ed47b3b1","digest":{"component_or_area":"close landed-work precheck","key_entities":["_referencing_commit_exists","resolve_ticket_id","src/rebar/_ids.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","tests/unit/test_transition_close.py","quiet parameter"],"problem_keywords":["precheck diagnostic noise","ambiguous prefix resolver","stderr pollution","commit scanning"],"propositions":["The close precheck scans all reachable commit messages and calls resolve_ticket_id for every extracted reference, causing ambiguous-prefix errors from unrelated historical commits to print to stderr even though the scan succeeds with a valid full ID elsewhere.","The resolver prints ambiguity diagnostics directly to stderr regardless of whether the caller (precheck scan loop) needs this output or will discard it.","Adding a quiet=False keyword parameter to resolve_ticket_id gates the three stderr ambiguity prints and allows precheck to pass quiet=True during history scans while preserving diagnostics for user-facing explicit ID resolution."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787344129880169923,"uuid":"340bd172-b3ba-4053-b273-8c9b6b9392e6"}